# Build context for the root Dockerfile: the broker only.
#
# Without this, a root-context build ships the whole repo — astro-starter,
# nextjs-starter, wp-plugin, docs, tests — to the daemon every time. Exclude
# everything, then re-admit hatch-deploy/.
#
# Both negation forms are here on purpose. Re-including a directory that `*`
# excluded is documented to bring its contents back, but the `/**` form is the
# unambiguous one and costs nothing. If the COPY ever fails with "not found",
# this pair is the first thing to look at.
#
# Later rules win, so the two secrets and node_modules are struck out AFTER the
# negation — order matters here.
*
!hatch-deploy
!hatch-deploy/**

hatch-deploy/node_modules
hatch-deploy/node_modules/**
hatch-deploy/.env
hatch-deploy/.env.*
hatch-deploy/npm-debug.log*
hatch-deploy/.img-cache
